 - Power: 12 W = 0.012 kW\n   - Monthly energy consumption: \\(0.012 \\, \\text{kW} \\times 100 \\, \\text{hours} = 1.2 \\, \\text{kWh}\\)\n   - Monthly cost: \\(1.2 \\, \\text{kWh} \\times 5 \\, \\text{rubles/kWh} = 6 \\, \\text{rubles}\\)\n   - Total cost over 10 months: \\(6 \\times 10 = 60 \\, \\text{rubles}\\)\n   - Upfront cost for the lamp: 120 rubles\n   - Total cost (self-install): \\(120 + 60 = 180 \\, \\text{rubles}\\)\n\n3. **Energy Service Company:**\n   - Savings over 10 months: \\(300 - 60 = 240 \\, \\text{rubles}\\)\n   - Company's share (75% of savings): \\(0.75 \\times 240 = 180 \\, \\text{rubles}\\)\n   - Resident's total cost: \\(60 + 180 = 240 \\, \\text{rubles}\\)\n\n**Conclusion for part (a):** The resident saves more by self-installing (180 rubles vs. 240 rubles).\n\n### Part (b): Entire lifespan of the energy-efficient lamp\n\nAssuming the lifespan of the energy-efficient lamp is \\( L \\) months:\n\n1. **Self-Install:**\n   - Total cost: \\(120 + 6L \\, \\text{rubles}\\)\n\n2. **Energy Service Company:**\n   - Cost for the first 10 months: 240 rubles\n   - Cost for the remaining \\( L - 10 \\) months: \\(6 \\times (L - 10)\\)\n   - Total cost: \\(240 + 6(L - 10) = 180 + 6L \\, \\text{rubles}\\)\n\n**Comparison:**\n- Self-install cost: \\(120 + 6L\\)\n- Company cost: \\(180 + 6L\\)\n\n**Conclusion for part (b):** The resident saves 60 rubles by self-installing regardless of the lifespan \\( L \\).\n\n### Final Answers\n\n(a) \\boxed{\\text{Install themselves}}\n\n(b) \\boxed{\\text{Install themselves}}", "ground_truth_solution": "\nConsider the problem of a city resident deciding whether to replace their old incandescent lamp with a more energy-efficient one or to install it through an energy service company.\n\n#### Part (a) Planning for 10 months\n\n1. **Calculate the cost of using a 60W incandescent lamp for 10 months:**\n\nGiven:\n   - Power usage, \\( P_1 = 60 \\, \\text{W} \\).\n   - Monthly usage time, \\( t = 100 \\, \\text{hours} \\).\n   - Tariff, \\( T = 5 \\, \\text{rubles/kWh} \\).\n   \n   Monthly energy consumption:\n   \\[\n   E_1 = \\frac{P_1 \\times t}{1000} = \\frac{60 \\, \\text{W} \\times 100 \\, \\text{hours}}{1000} = 6 \\, \\text{kWh}\n   \\]\n   \n   Monthly cost:\n   \\[\n   C_1 = E_1 \\times T = 6 \\, \\text{kWh} \\times 5 \\, \\text{rubles/kWh} = 30 \\, \\text{rubles}\n   \\]\n\n   Total cost for 10 months:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total cost}_1 = C_1 \\times 10 = 30 \\, \\text{rubles/month} \\times 10 = 300 \\, \\text{rubles}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the cost if the resident installs the 12W energy-efficient lamp himself:**\n\nGiven:\n   - Initial cost of the new lamp: 120 rubles.\n   - Power usage, \\( P_2 = 12 \\, \\text{W} \\).\n   \n   Monthly energy consumption:\n   \\[\n   E_2 = \\frac{P_2 \\times t}{1000} = \\frac{12 \\, \\text{W} \\times 100 \\, \\text{hours}}{1000} = 1.2 \\, \\text{kWh}\n   \\]\n   \n   Monthly cost:\n   \\[\n   C_2 = E_2 \\times T = 1.2 \\, \\text{kWh} \\times 5 \\, \\text{rubles/kWh} = 6 \\, \\text{rubles}\n   \\]\n\n   Total cost for 10 months:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total cost}_2 = \\text{Initial cost} + (\\text{monthly cost} \\times 10) = 120 \\, \\text{rubles} + (6 \\, \\text{rubles/month} \\times 10) = 120 \\, \\text{rubles} + 60 \\, \\text{rubles} = 180 \\, \\text{rubles}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the cost if the energy-efficient lamp is installed by the energy service company:**\n\nGiven:\n   - The energy savings would be the difference in consumption between the old and the new lamp:\n     \\[\n     \\Delta E = P_1 - P_2 = 60 \\, \\text{W} - 12 \\, \\text{W} = 48 \\, \\text{W}\n     \\]\n   \n   - Monthly energy savings:\n     \\[\n     \\Delta E \\times t = 48 \\, \\text{W} \\times 100 \\, \\text{hours} = 4800 \\, \\text{Wh} = 4.8 \\, \\text{kWh}\n     \\]\n   \n   - Monthly cost savings:\n     \\[\n     \\Delta C = 4.8 \\, \\text{kWh} \\times 5 \\, \\text{rubles/kWh} = 24 \\, \\text{rubles}\n     \\]\n   \n   - Payment to the energy service compa