ynomial \\(ax^2 + bx + c = 0\\) where \\(a > 0\\), the condition \\(f(a) < 0\\) ensures that \\(a\\) lies between the roots.\n\n5. **Evaluate \\( f(a) \\):**\n   Here, \\(f(a) = 2a^2 - 2016a + 2016^2 - 2016a - 1 - a^2\\):\n   \\[\n   f(a) = 2a^2 - 4032a + 2016^2 - 1 - a^2 = a^2 - 4032a + 2016^2 - 1.\n   \\]\n\n6. **Simplify \\( f(a) \\):**\n   \\[\n   f(a) = a^2 - 2 \\cdot 2016a + 2016^2 - 1\n   = (a - 2016)^2 - 1.\n   \\]\n\n7. **Set up the inequality \\( f(a) < 0 \\):**\n   \\[\n   (a - 2016)^2 - 1 < 0.\n   \\]\n\n8. **Solve the inequality:**\n   \\[\n   (a - 2016)^2 < 1 \\implies -1 < (a - 2016) < 1.\n   \\]\n   Adding 2016 to each part:\n   \\[\n   2015 < a < 2017.\n   \\]\n\n### Conclusion\nThe values of the parameter \\(a\\) that satisfy the given condition are:\n\\[ \\boxed{(2015, 2017)}. \\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "Given that \\( a_{1}, a_{2}, a_{3}, \\cdots, a_{1989}, a_{1990} \\) are all positive numbers. Also, let\n\n\\[ \n\\begin{array}{l}\nM=\\left(a_{1}+a_{2}+a_{3}+\\cdots+a_{1989}\\right)\\left(a_{2}+a_{3}+\\cdots+a_{1990}\\right) \\\\\nN=\\left(a_{1}+a_{2}+a_{3}+\\cdots+a_{1990}\\right)\\left(a_{2}+a_{3}+\\cdots+a_{1989}\\right)\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nThen, the relationship between \\( M \\) and \\( N \\) is:\n(A) \\( M = N \\).\n(B) \\( M < N \\).\n(C) \\( M > N \\).\n(D) The relationship is indeterminate.\n\n(From the Beijing High School Mathematics Competition, 1990)", "deepseek_reasoning": "Okay, so I have this problem here from the Beijing High School Mathematics Competition in 1990. Let me try to figure it out step by step. \n\nFirst, let me read the problem again to make sure I understand it. We have 1990 positive numbers: a\u2081, a\u2082, a\u2083, ..., up to a\u2081\u2089\u2089\u2080. Then they define two expressions, M and N:\n\nM is the product of (a\u2081 + a\u2082 + ... + a\u2081\u2089\u2088\u2089) and (a\u2082 + a\u2083 + ... + a\u2081\u2089\u2089\u2080).\n\nN i